# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# point-bang — environment reference for forks and self-hosted setups
#
# Read this first: NOTHING in this repo loads a .env file at runtime. This
# file documents (a) the secrets CI expects you to configure on GitHub and
# (b) the few environment variables the CLI honors as flag defaults. Copy it
# to `.env` only if your own tooling sources it; `.env` is gitignored so real
# tokens can never be committed.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── CI secrets ── configure these as GitHub Actions REPOSITORY SECRETS, not
# in a file: GitHub repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions →
# "New repository secret". The CI steps that use them skip gracefully while
# they are missing — the pipeline stays green, you just get no coverage/
# quality dashboards and the README badges show "unknown".

# Codecov upload token (ci.yml → codecov/codecov-action).
# Get it: https://codecov.io → log in with GitHub → add your fork → copy the
# repository upload token.
CODECOV_TOKEN=get-token-from-codecov

# SonarQube Cloud analysis token (ci.yml → sonarqube-scan-action).
# Get it: https://sonarcloud.io → log in with GitHub → import your fork →
# My Account → Security → Generate token.
# FORKS: also edit sonar-project.properties (sonar.projectKey and
# sonar.organization must match YOUR SonarCloud org/project) and the badge
# URLs in README.md and site/src/App.tsx.
SONAR_TOKEN=get-token-from-sonarqube

# ── Runtime (optional) ── the server is configured by CLI flags; these
# variables are honored only as DEFAULTS for the matching flag, mainly so a
# service manager can set them without editing a command line. Flags win.
# There is no dotenv loading — set them in the actual process environment.

# PORT=8443              # --port          http + ws (+ signaling)
# HTTPS_PORT=8444        # --https-port    https + wss when certs exist
# PREDICT_MS=0           # --predict-ms    aim extrapolation; 0 = off (default)
# PAUSE_COMBO=shift+space  # --pause-combo tracking-pause hotkey; "off" disables

# ── Not environment variables, but forks also need to know ──
# * ngrok (the --tunnel flow) authenticates via `ngrok config add-authtoken
#   <token>` (free account), not an env var.
# * The hosted pages (QR flow) live on GitHub Pages: enable Pages for your
#   fork (Settings → Pages → Source: GitHub Actions) and update the
#   hard-coded URLs — DEFAULT_PAGE_URL in lib/qr.ts, the origins in
#   site/src/App.tsx, docs/.vitepress/config.mts (base) and README.md — or
#   pass `--page-url https://<you>.github.io/<repo>/phone/` at runtime.
# * Releases: push a v* tag (`npm run release -- patch`, then
#   `git push origin main vX.Y.Z`) — no tokens needed beyond the automatic
#   GITHUB_TOKEN.
